  <story>
    <asA>developer</asA>
    <iWant>an agent that scans an existing project's file tree and generates wiki articles for every relevant source file</iWant>
    <soThat>existing projects can be brought into the knowledge graph without manual documentation</soThat>
    <tasks>
      <task id="1" ac="1,6">Create bootstrap pipeline definition
        <subtask>Define brownfield-bootstrap pipeline in the daemon pipeline registry with four sequential stages (scan, deps, decisions, populate)</subtask>
        <subtask>Create pipeline job type bootstrap in futurator-agent-jobs DynamoDB table schema</subtask>
        <subtask>Wire up pipeline event emission for progress tracking (scanning file X of Y)</subtask>
        <subtask>Add --project and --working-dir CLI arguments to the bootstrap entry point</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="2" ac="2,7,8">Implement file tree scanner
        <subtask>Create /home/ubuntu/scripts/bootstrap-scan.mjs — the scan orchestrator script</subtask>
        <subtask>Implement file discovery using Glob with configurable extension filters (.ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .py, .md, .json, .yaml, .yml, .sh, .css, .scss)</subtask>
        <subtask>Implement exclusion list: node_modules/, .git/, dist/, build/, .next/, coverage/, .mycelium/, knowledge/</subtask>
        <subtask>Sort discovered files by directory depth (process shallow files first for better dependency context)</subtask>
        <subtask>Chunk file list into batches of 10-20 for agent processing</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="3" ac="2,3,4">Implement wiki article generation agent step
        <subtask>Create agent prompt for the Knowledge Compiler role — reads source files and generates wiki articles following the standard article format from architecture doc section 3.1</subtask>
        <subtask>For each file in a batch: read file content, analyze purpose, identify exports/functions, detect imports, infer signals and missing signals</subtask>
        <subtask>Generate frontmatter with: title (source path), type: code, phase: implementation, status: active, maturity: 0.5, created/updated dates, tags (inferred from content)</subtask>
        <subtask>Use file naming convention: knowledge/code/{slug}.md where slug uses -- for path separators (e.g., src--components--auth.tsx.md)</subtask>
        <subtask>Generate preliminary [[wikilinks]] based on detected import statements</subtask>
        <subtask>Allowed agent tools: Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="4" ac="1,5">Initialize wiki structure and populate index
        <subtask>Call init-wiki.sh ${projectId} ${workingDir} to create directory structure before scanning begins</subtask>
        <subtask>After all batches complete, generate knowledge/index.md with the complete catalog (title, type, status, path for each article)</subtask>
        <subtask>Generate initial knowledge/log.md entry recording the bootstrap scan (timestamp, file count, article count)</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="5" ac="6,8">Progress tracking and error handling
        <subtask>Emit pipeline events after each batch completes: { type: progress, stage: scan, batch: N, total: M, filesProcessed: X }</subtask>
        <subtask>Implement retry logic for individual file failures (skip file, log error, continue)</subtask>
        <subtask>Write scan manifest to .mycelium/bootstrap-manifest.json with list of all scanned files and their generated article paths</subtask>
        <subtask>Log total scan duration and cost estimate to knowledge/log.md</subtask>
      </task>
    </tasks>
  </story>

  <acceptanceCriteria>
    <criterion id="1">Given an existing project at /home/ubuntu/projects/{name}/ with source code but no knowledge/ directory, the scan agent initializes the wiki directory structure using the init-wiki.sh script (Story 1.3)</criterion>
    <criterion id="2">For each relevant source file (filtered by extension: .ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .py, .md, .json, etc.), a wiki article is created in knowledge/code/ with Purpose, Key Exports, Dependencies, Dependents, Signals, and Missing Signals sections</criterion>
    <criterion id="3">Articles include correct frontmatter: type code, phase implementation, status active, maturity 0.5 (reverse-engineered, not authored)</criterion>
    <criterion id="4">[[wikilinks]] connect files that import each other (preliminary — refined in Story 6.2)</criterion>
    <criterion id="5">knowledge/index.md is populated with the complete catalog of generated articles</criterion>
    <criterion id="6">Progress is emitted as pipeline events for UI tracking (percentage complete, current file)</criterion>
    <criterion id="7">Files in node_modules/, .git/, dist/, build/, .next/, and other generated directories are excluded</criterion>
    <criterion id="8">The agent processes files in batches of 10-20 to manage context window and avoid token limits</criterion>
  </acceptanceCriteria>

