  <constraints>
    <constraint type="performance">Heavy-lift operation: 100-500 source files, 5-30 minutes duration, ~$0.50-2.00 in API calls. Batching is essential — 10-20 files per agent call to stay within context windows.</constraint>
    <constraint type="maturity">Brownfield articles start at maturity 0.5 (lower than greenfield 0.7) because they are reverse-engineered, not authored. Users refine later.</constraint>
    <constraint type="infrastructure">Runs on EC2 t4g.small (2GB RAM). Must share resources with Memgraph (~512MB) and daemon (~100MB). File processing is I/O-bound, not memory-bound.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">Wiki markdown files are the source of truth. Memgraph is rebuilt from wiki content. All generated articles must follow the standard format from architecture doc section 3.1.</constraint>
    <constraint type="exclusion">Must exclude: node_modules/, .git/, dist/, build/, .next/, coverage/, .mycelium/, knowledge/. These are generated directories that should never be scanned.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependencies">Requires Epic 1 complete: Memgraph running (1.1), schema initialized (1.2), wiki structure (1.3), Voyage AI (1.4), graph-sync (1.5). This is the first story in Epic 6.</constraint>
  </constraints>

